  "dct_description_sm": [
    "The ultimate purpose of collecting photographs of killer whales in the Canadian Arctic is to identify individual whales using unique markings on the dorsal fin and saddle patch and to track these individuals over time. Eventually, this will allow us to estimate patterns of distribution and abundance and to understand group structure and the overall natural history of Arctic killer whales."
